<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31325" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nūbĭgĕna</span></b> ,
		ae, comm.
		nubes-gigno, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>cloud-born, born of clouds</i> or <i>of a cloud</i> (<b>poet.</b>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 1, 365</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nimbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Hamart. 486</span></i>
			: clipei, <i>the Ancilia</i> (so called because
			they fell from the sky), <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 2,
			131</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The Centaurs</i>, whom Ixion begot of a cloud,
				<i><span class="en">Stat.
				Th. 5, 263</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12, 211</span></i>; <i><span class="en">541</span></i>;
			cf. <i><span class="en">Hyg.
				Fab. 62</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Phrixus</i>, as the son of Nephele: Phrixus
			nubigena, Col. poët. 10, 115.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
